{
  "observation": "The driver waits for real SDK IME and published keyboard measurements, then actually scrolls until complete native input/save rectangles are above IME. It never synthesizes keyboard metrics or hides IME to pass. Seven complete rows/161 native page frames and all 63 keyboard combinations were independently reinspected; only eight clipped historical save proofs received targeted real native supplementary observations. Native desktop boundary recovery at width 768 was actually verified. Reviewed functions are byte identical to the executed native proposal; generated original matrix assertions remain unchanged by inverse transformation. Product code, requirements, planning originals and all 206 earlier valid visits remain unaffected. Closing this repair only permits an actual rerun of the two remaining configurations and desktop boundary.",
